==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|erda|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|erþō|lang=gem-pro}}. Compare Dutch {{term|aarde|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|ierde|lang=fy}}, English {{term|earth|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|jord|lang=da}}, Gothic {{term|𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌸𐌰|tr=airþa|lang=got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʔeːɐ̯də/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|de-Erde.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|eːɐ̯də|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|gen=Erde|pl=Erden|g=f}}

# the planet [[Earth]]
# [[soil]]
#: {{usex|Sie nahm eine Handvoll '''Erde'''.|t=She took a handful of soil.|lang=de|inline=1}}
# the [[ground]]
#: {{usex|Er fiel auf die '''Erde'''.|t=He fell on the ground.|lang=de|inline=1}}

